WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.807
You've spent years building
your YouTube channel.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.585
Maybe you have five thousand subscribers.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.613
Maybe twenty thousand.

00:00:07.911 --> 00:00:11.907
But your long videos aren't always
reaching as many people as you'd hoped.

00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:14.691
You've thought about turning them
into Shorts.

00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:16.566
There's just one problem.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.950
Time.

00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:21.300
You're already spending hours planning,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.578
recording, editing, and uploading
your long videos.

00:00:24.811 --> 00:00:26.304
And as soon as one is finished,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.720
you're working on the next.

00:00:28.292 --> 00:00:30.025
Now add Shorts to that.

00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:33.600
Finding the right moments, cutting clips,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.200
adding captions, fixing the framing,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.727
and scheduling posts across YouTube,
Instagram, and Facebook.

00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:42.457
Maybe you've tried AI clipping tools.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.840
Some clips are good.

00:00:44.231 --> 00:00:45.599
Others miss the point.

00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:47.793
The tools can create clips,

00:00:48.001 --> 00:00:51.427
but someone still has to decide which ones
are worth publishing.

00:00:52.024 --> 00:00:53.707
You could hire a freelancer,

00:00:53.974 --> 00:00:57.644
but then you're managing deadlines,
feedback, and availability.

00:00:58.169 --> 00:00:59.897
An agency could handle more,

00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:02.006
but the costs add up quickly.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:04.970
So you post Shorts for a few weeks,

00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:07.761
get busy, and eventually stop.

00:01:08.271 --> 00:01:09.758
Not because you don't want to.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.494
You just don't have the time.

00:01:12.211 --> 00:01:15.269
Now imagine someone else takes care
of the Shorts.

00:01:15.676 --> 00:01:17.523
Like having your own editing team,

00:01:17.822 --> 00:01:19.473
without the agency price tag.

00:01:19.969 --> 00:01:21.506
It works in three steps.

00:01:21.961 --> 00:01:25.976
First, you keep uploading your long
videos, just like you already do.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.323
Every time a new video goes live,

00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:30.289
it's picked up automatically.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.949
A video editor uses AI to identify
potential clips,

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.059
then reviews them one by one.

00:01:36.575 --> 00:01:39.225
They check where each Short should start
and end,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.098
choose the opening hook, and take care
of captions, titles, and design.

00:01:44.644 --> 00:01:45.762
Once the Shorts are ready,

00:01:46.061 --> 00:01:47.514
they're sent to you for review.

00:01:48.153 --> 00:01:50.425
Second, you watch and approve.

00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:52.804
You get an email when the Shorts
are ready.

00:01:53.298 --> 00:01:56.493
You watch them, approve the ones you like,
and skip the rest.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.403
Nothing gets published unless
you approve it.

00:02:00.063 --> 00:02:03.018
Third, the approved Shorts
go out on schedule.

00:02:03.513 --> 00:02:07.958
They get published to your connected
YouTube and Instagram accounts

00:02:08.432 --> 00:02:09.481
at the scheduled times.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.204
And at the end of the month,
you receive a report

00:02:12.462 --> 00:02:14.300
showing how they performed, including

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.370
views, engagement, and subscriber trends
where available.

00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:18.839
The next time you upload a long video,

00:02:19.051 --> 00:02:20.923
the same process happens again.

00:02:21.438 --> 00:02:24.460
And that's how you can maintain
a consistent Shorts schedule

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.230
without doing all the extra work yourself.
